Defects found:

- Line 46, idempotency guard satisfied by its own marker.  
  Exact input: `<!-- Contributor Roles (CRediT) --><tr><td class="p-4 font-bold text-slate-400">Conflicts of Interest</td><td class="p-4 text-slate-300">None</td></tr>`  
  Consequence: `patch()` returns `ALREADY`, so neither required disclosure row is inserted.

- Lines 21-23, selector keyed to an overly exact HTML form.  
  Exact input: `<tr>\n<td class="p-4 font-bold text-slate-400">Conflicts of Interest</td><td class="p-4 text-slate-300">None</td></tr>`  
  Consequence: valid equivalent HTML returns `NO_COI_ROW`, so the injection silently does not happen.

- Lines 49-50 / 77, status code reports wrapper success rather than work success.  
  Exact input: one file `x_REVIEW.html` containing `<html></html>`, then run `python scripts/inject_credit_block.py`.  
  Consequence: the script exits `0` even though no target row was found or patched.

- Lines 59-60 / 77, check cannot fail when the corpus selection is empty.  
  Exact input: no files matching `*_REVIEW.html` under `REPO`.  
  Consequence: the script exits `0` after “Patching 0 review HTMLs ...”, so a missing corpus is indistinguishable from successful completion to CI.

